e and the approximate double bottom with 2357.18, weakening the Always-In Long read and supporting a larger trading range 2357.18-2850.", "Range development: five or more further bars overlapping inside 2633.31-2786.81 without a new high would turn the pause into a trading range at the highs and lower Always-In relevance."], "window_bars": 120}, "freshness": "current"}, "H4": {"context": {"always_in": "long", "always_in_relevance": "low", "breakout_mode": true, "confidence": "medium", "decision_time_ms": 1790423999999, "directional_pressure": "bull", "evidence_against": ["Strongest counterargument: the last 30 bars (90-119) are two-sided inside 2633.31-2804.59 and step to lower highs (2804.59, then 2786.81, then 2740.42) with the last 6 bars compressed into 2669.67-2721.75 on 2-3M volume, so the current state reads as a trading range, or a possible final flag, rather than an active bull phase - a 'trading-range' primary regime is a plausible alternative.", "The window's earlier bear leg (2609.02 to 2358.62, bars 50-55) is comparable in size to the bull legs, so on 120 bars the market can equally be framed as a wide range 2358.62-2850 with a bull bias.", "Bar 89's long upper tail and the failure of any later close to exceed 2775.61 show the move above 2700-2804.59 was not accepted at the highs.", "The pullback retraces roughly 45% of the 2370.54-2850 advance over about 30 bars with heavy overlap; a bull trend break plus a lower high below 2804.59 followed by bar 102's break to 2648.49 gives a candidate mtr-like top shape, though no follow-through below 2633.31 has appeared."], "evidence_for": ["Higher-high/higher-low progression since the bar 55 low 2358.62 (lows 2370.54, 2568.16, 2633.31; highs 2643.52, 2700, 2850) is the signature of a bull trend, and the advance accepted above prior range tops (2530.36 bar 47, 2544.63 bar 49) and above 2700 (bars 77 and 87).", "The pullback since bar 89 has held above the 2568.16 higher low and only about 65 points above the 2643.52 breakout high (bar 73), which is a normal test of a breakout point rather than a bear reversal.", "Bar 102's bear break (low 2648.49) had no follow-through; bars 103-113 traded back up to 2715.9-2740.42, lows after bar 107 rise (2640, 2660.49, 2673.88, 2667.22, 2671.18, 2669.67, 2678.27, 2679.27), and the last close 2689.42 is above the window midpoint.", "The strongest displacement in the window is the roughly 480-point up leg from 2358.62/2370.54 to 2850, with closes on the upper half of the 120-bar range even after the pullback."], "missing_information": [], "observations": ["120 closed H4 bars; window low 2358.62 (bar 55), window high 2850 (bar 89); last close 2689.42 is above the window midpoint near 2604 and above the first bar close 2478.43.", "After bar 55 low 2358.62 the swing lows rise: 2370.54 (bar 61), 2568.16 (bar 83), 2633.31 (bar 107); swing highs rise: 2643.52 (bar 73), 2700 (bar 77), 2850 (bar 89).", "Bar 89 (open 2658.81, low 2658.06, high 2850, close 2723.15, volume 8,427,249) covered 192 points, closed in the lower third of its range and left roughly a 127-point upper tail; no later close exceeds 2775.61 (bar 92).", "Bar 102 (open 2726.71, high 2727.77, low 2648.49, close 2659) broke below the 2716.01-2804.59 stretch of bars 90-101, but bar 103 closed 2676.47 and bars 103-113 traded back up to a 2740.42 high (bar 113).", "Bars 90-119 overlap inside 2633.31-2804.59; bars 102-119 hold inside 2633.31-2740.42 and the last 6 bars (114-119) hold inside 2669.67-2721.75 with closes between 2671.19 and 2715.9.", "Volume falls from 10,757,237.648 (bar 30), 10,207,100.424 (bar 55) and 8,427,249.993 (bar 89) to 3,360,194.836 (bar 117), 2,083,949.406 (bar 118) and 2,891,333.518 (bar 119).", "The 2370.54-2850 advance is about 480 points; the 2633.31 pullback low retraces roughly 45% of it, sits 65 points above the 2568.16 higher low (bar 83) and is close to the 2643.52 breakout high (bar 73)."], "phase": "range", "primary_regime": "bull-trend", "role": "CONTEXT_ANALYST", "schema": "brooks.market-context.v2", "structures": [{"description": "Early two-sided stretch (bars 0-29): repeated pushes into 2517-2528.8 and dips into 2462-2411.04, with overlapping bars and several closes near the open; no acceptance beyond either edge.", "end_time_ms": 1789127999999, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "2411.04", "start_time_ms": 1788696000000, "upper_boundary": "2528.8"}, {"description": "Bull spike/breakout attempt (bars 30-31): bar 30 opened 2457.12, ran to 2680 and closed 2555.52 on 10.76M volume, above the prior 29-bar highs; bar 31 reached 2607.62. Bars 32-33 gave the spike back to 2511.99, so the 2607-2680 extreme was not accepted.", "end_time_ms": 1789156799999, "kind": "breakout", "lower_boundary": "2444.19", "start_time_ms": 1789128000000, "upper_boundary": "2680"}, {"description": "Bear leg (bars 50-55): bar 50 (open 2540.11, high 2609.02, close 2514.07) reversed an intraday push to 2609.02, and bars 51-55 stepped down to the window low 2358.62 with 9-10M volume on bars 54 and 55.", "end_time_ms": 1789502399999, "kind": "swing", "lower_boundary": "2358.62", "start_time_ms": 1789416000000, "upper_boundary": "2609.02"}, {"description": "Bull leg (bars 55-89) with higher lows 2370.54 (bar 61) and 2568.16 (bar 83) and higher highs 2643.52 (bar 73), 2700 (bar 77) and 2850 (bar 89); it contains a two-bar spike at bars 72-73 and an overlapping ~75-point pullback into bar 83 before the final push.", "end_time_ms": 1789991999999, "kind": "channel", "lower_boundary": "2358.62", "start_time_ms": 1789488000000, "upper_boundary": "2850"}, {"description": "Bar 89 (open 2658.81, low 2658.06, high 2850, close 2723.15) is the largest bar of the bull leg with a long upper tail and a close near the lower third of its range - a buy-climax/exhaustion candidate at the window high.", "end_time_ms": 1789991999999, "kind": "climax", "lower_boundary": "2658.06", "start_time_ms": 1789977600000, "upper_boundary": "2850"}, {"description": "Post-spike trading range (bars 90-119): highs 2804.59 (bar 92), 2786.81 (bar 100) and 2740.42 (bar 113) step lower while lows hold 2633.31 (bar 107), above the 2568.16 higher low; bar 102's bear break (low 2648.49) had no follow-through, and the last 6 bars trade inside 2669.67-2721.75 on shrinking volume.", "end_time_ms": 1790423999999, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "2633.31", "start_time_ms": 1789992000000, "upper_boundary": "2804.59"}], "symbol": "ETH-USDT", "timeframe": "H4", "transition_conditions": ["Bull resolution: a close above 2740.42 (bar 113 high) followed by a close above 2804.59 (bar 92 high) with expanding ranges on the up bars would move the phase toward breakout-spike; a close above 2850 would confirm resumption of the higher-high sequence.", "Bear resolution: a close below 2633.31 (bar 107 low) with follow-through, particularly after a lower high under 2804.59, would break the higher-low sequence and the 2643.52 breakout-point test, shifting the read toward a bear leg or transition and making the mtr-like interpretation credible.", "Range persistence: continued closes inside roughly 2660-2700 with overlapping small bars and no acceptance above 2740.42 or below 2633.31 would keep the range phase and low Always-In relevance.", "Failed upper test: rejection at 2804.59 that reverses with a strong bear bar would keep the range's upper boundary intact and shift directional pressure toward balanced."], "window_bars": 120}, "freshness": "stale"}}, "raw": {"H1": [{"close": "2753.69", "close_time_ms": 1790009999999, "high": "2765.34", "low": "2742", "open": "2754.31", "open_time_ms": 1790006400000, "volume": "2251502.362"}, {"close": "2740.89", "close_time_ms": 1790013599999, "high": "2755.18", "low": "2734.22", "open": "2753.69", "open_time_ms": 1790010000000, "volume": "1847680.376"}, {"close": "2756.61", "close_time_ms": 1790017199999, "high": "2756.72", "low": "2737.86", "open": "2740.89", "open_time_ms": 1790013600000, "volume": "1726337.379"}, {"close": "